#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:1
msgid "Types & Traits"
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:3
msgid "Use types to enforce invariants (`rust-type-invariants`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:5
msgid "Leverage the type system to make illegal states _unrepresentable_."
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:8
msgid "Define newtypes to encode domain constraints."
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:11
msgid "// Good — a `Nice` value is guaranteed to be valid\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:14
msgid "// Bad — `i8` admits invalid values for nice levels\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:19
msgid "Prefer enums over bare integers and boolean flags."
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:22
msgid "// Good — access mode is constrained by the enum\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:29
msgid "// Bad — `u8` admits invalid values\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:34
msgid "Encode invariants in generic parameters where needed."
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:38
msgid "// Good — only unsafe code can write to sensitive MMIO\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:39
#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:44
msgid "/* .. */"
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:43
msgid "// Good — safe code can write to insensitive MMIO\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:51
msgid ""
"Asterinas uses this pattern widely, for example with newtypes such as "
"`CpuId` and `AlignedUsize<const N: u16>`."
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:55
msgid ""
"See also: PR [\\#2265](https://github.com/asterinas/asterinas/pull/"
"2265#discussion_r2266214191) and [\\#2514](https://github.com/asterinas/"
"asterinas/pull/2514)."
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:59
msgid "Prefer enum over trait objects for closed sets (`enum-over-dyn`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:61
msgid ""
"When the set of variants is known and closed, an enum is often preferable to "
"`Box<dyn Trait>` for both performance and pattern-matching expressiveness."
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:66
msgid "// Good — closed set modeled as an enum\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:74
msgid "Encapsulate fields behind getters (`getter-encapsulation`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:76
msgid ""
"Do not make fields public when a simple getter method would do. A getter "
"preserves naming flexibility and leaves room for future invariants."
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:82
msgid "// Good — field is private, accessed via getter\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:92
msgid "// Bad — public field exposes representation\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:99
msgid ""
"Define bit flags types outside the macro for custom derives (`bitflags-"
"derives`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:101
msgid ""
"When a bit flags type needs a custom derive that `bitflags` does not "
"natively support, define an integer wrapper outside `bitflags!` and use the "
"macro's `impl` syntax to generate the flags API."
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:107
msgid "/// Device status flags serialized in a reply.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:120
msgid ""
"See also: [`bitflags` custom derives](https://docs.rs/bitflags/2.13.0/"
"bitflags/#custom-derives) and issue [\\#4120](https://github.com/asterinas/"
"asterinas/issues/4120)."
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:124
msgid "Keep bit flags declarations consistent (`bitflags-layout`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:126
msgid ""
"Use spaces to align the `=` signs and values within each flags type, "
"including unnamed masks."
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:129
msgid ""
"Within each flags type, use either bit shifts or numeric literals "
"consistently. Zero values and unnamed masks are exempt, as are composite "
"expressions and references to other flags."
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:135
msgid "/// Access permissions for a mapping.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:147
msgid "Declare the bits that `bitflags` must retain (`bitflags-retained-bits`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:149
msgid ""
"In a `bitflags!` declaration, use an unnamed mask for uninterpreted bits "
"that must be retained: use `const _ = !0;` for all bits, or a narrower mask "
"for a subset. Explain which bit patterns the type accepts next to the mask."
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:155
msgid "/// A register snapshot used for read-modify-write updates.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:160
msgid ""
"// This type accepts all bit patterns,\n"
"        // although only some flags are recognized.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:167
msgid ""
"With `const _ = !0`, `from_bits` accepts every bit pattern, so callers must "
"check supported options separately when required."
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-maintainability/rust-specific/types-and-traits.md:170
msgid ""
"See also: [`bitflags` externally defined flags](https://docs.rs/bitflags/"
"2.13.0/bitflags/#externally-defined-flags)."
msgstr ""
